 ## Overview
-MultiVariateTransferFunction maps multiple input data fields to RGBA optical properties using separate transfer function tables and explicit channel linking [S1, unofficial][S3]. It solves the problem of combining distinct physical quantities (e.g., temperature and density) into a single coherent visualization, allowing for complex weightings and linkages that single-field methods cannot express [S2, S3]. It is distinguished from [1D Transfer Function](11719-1d-transfer-function.md) by its ability to handle multi-dimensional input domains through modular table assignment and channel routing [S1, unofficial][S3].
+MultiVariateTransferFunction maps multiple input data fields to RGBA optical properties using separate transfer function tables and explicit channel linking [S1, unofficial][S3]. It solves the problem of combining distinct physical quantities (e.g., temperature and density) into a single coherent visualization, allowing for complex weightings and linkages that single-field methods cannot express [S2, S3]. It builds on [Classification and transfer functions](38-classification-and-transfer-functions.md) and is distinguished from [1D Transfer Function](11719-1d-transfer-function.md) by its ability to handle multi-dimensional input domains through modular table assignment and channel routing [S1, unofficial][S3].
 
